<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Technical University of Darmstadt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1877">1877</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as TU Darmstadt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Technical University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> is a German university of technology in Darmstadt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. It grew from a higher trade school founded in 1836 and became a technical university in 1877. In 1882 it established a chair of electrical engineering, often described as the first in the world, and it is today one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/technical-university">technical universities</a>.</p></div>
